        <mxCell id="ch0u" value="128" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#3E4652;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="850" y="714" width="104" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="cap" value="Figure 1. Score-based generative modelling through SDEs, drawn from the repository at commit cb1f359. (a) A forward SDE takes data x(0) to noise; the three families in sde_lib.py differ only in f and g, and d(t) = 1 - exp(-2 B(t)) is the sub-VP discount. The network is trained by denoising score matching on the perturbed sample. (b) The same SDE run backwards in time generates samples: one corrector step then one predictor step per timestep, repeated N = 1000 times; the probability flow ODE is the deterministic alternative and also yields exact likelihoods in bits/dim. (c) The score network for the ve/cifar10_ncsnpp_continuous configuration. Block width is the spatial resolution, written inside each block; the bold number below each block is the channel count; × 4 and × 5 are the numbers of BigGAN residual blocks in the encoder and decoder. Attention is applied at 16² only. The time embedding is added inside every residual block; the single green arrow stands for that shared conditioning. Not drawn: FIR up and downsampling, skip rescaling and the residual input pyramid (progressive_input = residual), all of which are configuration flags rather than separate stages." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Times New Roman;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#3C4350;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="890" width="940" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
